From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:50:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(ui): smooth category paging and share animation clock
 protection

Shared animation policy and regression tests with Mihon 0082. The user reports smoother inertia after preview.33 but stuttering horizontal category swipes. Pager snapping and explicit page transitions previously bypassed the fling clock protection, and currentPage changes persisted preferences/rebuilt active state before the gesture settled. Protect native targeted pager flings while forwarding remaining-distance updates, protect explicit page animations, observe settledPage for persistence, and resolve category item lists on the existing background grouping pipeline so getters return stable lists. Apply the same clock policy to custom category indicators, scrolling category strips, navigation movement/press feedback and scroller fades, preserving their timing, retargeting and visual styling. Cover all existing native pagers in these apps. Add real Compose regression for bidirectional swipes, settled-only persistence, rapid page retargeting and intermediate indicator animation. This addresses confirmed repeated work and the unprotected animation path; no timing log for this new symptom or measured FPS gain is claimed.
